\viewkind4\uc1\pard\tx3780\tx3960\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Crown Him with many crowns, 
\par The Lamb upon His throne ;
\par Hark ! how the heavenly anthem drowns
\par All music but  its own :
\par Awake, my soul, and sing 
\par Of Him who died for thee,
\par And hail Him as thy matchless King
\par Though all eternity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Crow Him the Lord of life.
\par Who triumphed o'er the grave
\par And rose victorious in the strife
\par For those He came to save ;
\par His glories now we sing
\par Who died and roseon high
\par Who died-eternal life to bring,
\par And lives, that death may die.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Crown Him the Lord of peace,
\par Whose power a scepter sways
\par From pole to pole, that wars may cease,
\par And all be prayer and praise:
\par His reign shall know no end,
\par And round His pierced feet
\par Fair flowers of paradise extend
\par Their fragrance ever sweet.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Crow Him the Lord of love ;
\par Behold His hands and side,
\par Those wounds, yet visible above,
\par In beauty glorified :
\par All hail, Redeemer, hail !
\par For Thou hast died for me :
\par Thy praise and glory shall not fail
\par Throughout eternity.\tab 
\par                          Amen.
\par \pard 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f1 
